# Thesis Requirements - Stockholm University

** :** Praveen Kumar Donta  
**Topic:** Distributed Agentic Micro-Agent for Resilience in the Computing Continuum

## Core Requirements (MUST FOLLOW)

### 1. Multiple Small Micro-Agents (NOT one big LLM)
- Each agent performs ONE small intelligent task
- Runs on resource-constrained devices (Raspberry Pi, IoT, edge)
- Examples: BandwidthCheckAgent, CameraTrafficAgent, NodeLoadAgent, NetworkDelayAgent

### 2. CCTV Use Case (EXACT scenario)
- Raspberry Pi processing live CCTV security camera footage at edge
- SLOs: 30 FPS, delay < 33ms, throughput > 1.6 MB/s, success rate ≥95%
- Fault: Network congestion → FPS drop, delay spike to 80ms, throughput drop

### 3. Root Cause Identification (CRITICAL - Two-Step Process)

**STEP 1:** Identify EXACT root cause using Bayesian Networks
  - Example causes: "Camera #3 sending excessive frames", "bandwidth drop on link", "node overloaded"
  - Use pgmpy Bayesian Network from Sedlak et al. (2024)
  - Multiple parallel agents provide consensus
  - Must achieve HIGH CERTAINTY (≥85%)

**STEP 2:** Apply VFE check AFTER root cause proposal
  - VFE below threshold confirms it is safe to act
  - Only proceed if VFE < threshold

**STEP 3:** Execute healing action (rebalance, offload, switch endpoint, isolate node)

### 4. Foundation Papers
- **Sedlak et al. (2024)** "Equilibrium in Computing Continuum through Active Inference"
  - Use pgmpy Bayesian Network structure
  - Agent/FogNode classes
  - Markov blankets, causal diagnosis
  
- **Donta et al. (2025)** "Resilient by Design" (arXiv:2511.07202)
  - PAIR-Agent concepts for causal fault graphs
  - VFE-based certainty on root cause

